                        "entry_id": "9410d7f3-5cae-35af-8f29-8d94482c6af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In bryophytes, a thin hood of tissue that forms from the archegonium and covers the developing sporophyte and is shed as it ripens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b198d8a7-c96a-40fc-92d7-addcae41ccf5",
                                "sense_id": "21d4c73b-590b-3a10-afdf-7b57e50d72d1",
                                "text": "(b) sporophyte with foot reduced, the entire sporophyte enveloped by the calyptra, which is ± stipitate at the base."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4bb815b9-9fb9-3ec0-acb9-71c14650c9fc",
                        "entry_id": "9410d7f3-5cae-35af-8f29-8d94482c6af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "any cap-like covering of a flower or fruit, such as the operculum over the unopened buds of Eucalyptus flowers"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
